cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the HD 11964 pilot data or validation tables, please cite them as below, together
  with the orbital solution they pin (references).
type: dataset
title: "HD11964-PILOT: pinned planar three-body model of HD 11964 and its drift-certificate gate"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-01
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - family-names: Armstrong
    given-names: Scott
    affiliation: "CNRS, Sorbonne Université, Courant Institute"
  - family-names: Komargodski
    given-names: Zohar
repository-code: "https://github.com/"  # KAM-dev repository URL to be filled in by the owner
keywords:
  - celestial mechanics
  - planetary three-body problem
  - angular momentum deficit
  - normal forms
  - computer-assisted proof
  - HD 11964
abstract: >-
  Pinned inputs (exact rationals with catalogue provenance) of a planar Newtonian model of the
  HD 11964 system (star, planets c and b, minimum masses, coplanar), and the numerical gate of a
  planned Lean certificate of a no-orbit-crossing time: a fast-angle Lie normal form with the slow
  variables, and its drift rate measured against the original Hamiltonian over the whole AMD ball.
  Funded by the European Research Council (ERC), grant agreement No. 101200828.
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Rosenthal
        given-names: Lee J.
      - name: "et al."
    title: "The California Legacy Survey. I. A Catalog of 178 Planets from Precision Radial Velocity Monitoring of 719 Nearby Stars over Three Decades"
    journal: "The Astrophysical Journal Supplement Series"
    volume: 255
    issue: 1
    start: 8
    year: 2021
    doi: 10.3847/1538-4365/abe23c
  - type: database
    title: "NASA Exoplanet Archive, Planetary Systems table"
    url: "https://exoplanetarchive.ipac.caltech.edu/"
    date-accessed: 2026-11-01
